From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:18:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: connac: don't take the station TX rate from
 fixed-rate TXS

mt7915 requests a TX status report for one frame per station every
250 ms, and mac80211 requests them for various management frames.
When that frame is sent at a fixed rate (management, multicast or
IEEE80211_TX_CTL_USE_MINRATE frames such as EAPOL),
mt76_connac2_mac_fill_txs() still stores the reported legacy rate in
wcid->rate. That rate is reported to mac80211 as the last TX rate for
the station, which shows up in station dumps and feeds the airtime
estimates used by AQL, until the next status report replaces it.

The TXS already says whether the frame used a fixed rate, so skip the
wcid->rate update for those frames and keep the statistics.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt76_connac_mac.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/mt76_connac_mac.c b/mt76_connac_mac.c
index 5fff968a..b80bdf0f 100644
--- a/mt76_connac_mac.c
+++ b/mt76_connac_mac.c
@@ -746,7 +746,14 @@ bool mt76_connac2_mac_fill_txs(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct mt76_wcid *wcid,
 		stats->tx_bw[0]++;
 		break;
 	}
-	wcid->rate = rate;
+
+	/* Management, multicast and min-rate frames go out at a fixed
+	 * rate that doesn't reflect rate control, so don't let their
+	 * status overwrite the rate used for reporting and airtime
+	 * estimation.
+	 */
+	if (!(txs & MT_TXS0_FIXED_RATE))
+		wcid->rate = rate;
 
 	return true;
 }
